cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "StressTestRAG: A Human-Annotated Benchmark for Software Reliability Testing of Retrieval-Augmented Generation under Crisis-Induced Prompt Noise"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: ""
    family-names: ""
    affiliation: ""
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-03"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  StressTestRAG is a human-annotated benchmark for evaluating the reliability of
  Retrieval-Augmented Generation systems when user queries preserve semantic
  intent but exhibit crisis-induced linguistic noise, such as anxiety, panic,
  urgency, fragmentation, typographical error, and distrust. Each scenario pairs
  a calm baseline question with five stressed variants, all linked to an evidence
  chunk from an official source document.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - software reliability testing
  - robustness evaluation
  - human annotation
  - crisis communication
